      <S N="Description">The Get-WhatsNew cmdlet allows you to see What's New information from the release notes for_x000D__x000A_PowerShell. By default it shows the release notes for the current version of PowerShell you are_x000D__x000A_running. You can also provide a specific version or a range of versions to be displayed._x000D__x000A__x000D__x000A_The cmdlet can display release notes for the following versions of PowerShell_x000D__x000A_- Windows PowerShell 5.1_x000D__x000A_- PowerShell 6.0_x000D__x000A_- PowerShell 6.1_x000D__x000A_- PowerShell 6.2_x000D__x000A_- PowerShell 7.0_x000D__x000A_- PowerShell 7.1_x000D__x000A_- PowerShell 7.2_x000D__x000A_- PowerShell 7.3_x000D__x000A_- PowerShell 7.4_x000D__x000A_- PowerShell 7.5 (preview)_x000D__x000A__x000D__x000A_By default, the cmdlet shows all of the release notes for a version. You can also limit it to_x000D__x000A_display a single random section of the release notes. This can be used as a "Message of the Day".</S>
